@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# C1/C2 GC type-capacity fix — 2026-10-31
+
+Branch: `fix/typecap-c1c2`
+
+Implementation commit: `059d10f` (`Grow WebAssembly GC type metadata on registration`)
+
+## Change
+
+- `gc/wasm_adapter.goose`: replaced both 4,096-entry canonical maps and checked-type arrays with store-owned growable scoped storage. Registration computes both required extents, grows only before the transactional registration, preserves the zero type sentinel, refreshes collector configuration/views, and accounts for new type metadata. `wasm_gc_type` remains a direct indexed read.
+- `src/jit.goose`: `run_file` and `spec_session` now own the scoped type and canonical-map backing for both collector ABIs and publish their flat pointer/length views to the native boundary.
+- `src/jit_gc.goose`: all collector entry points consistently reopen those views; module registration republishes views after possible growth, linked/native lookup uses the supplied map, and close, root, constant, and execution paths retain the same store-owned lifetime.
+- `native/jit_linux_x86_64.S`: native ABI shims reconstruct the scoped type/map slices from the flat owner pointer/length fields before entering Goose, preserving flat native ownership.
+- `tests/test_gc_type_capacity.py`: retained the 4,097- and 20,000-type early-managed regressions and added C1 canonical IDs 4,095/4,096 plus C2 managed-layout counts 4,095/4,096 for every release, debug, and three-byte runner.
+- `Makefile`: runs the capacity suite through release, debug, and three-byte builds.
+- `gc/api.goose`: unchanged. Its overflow/capacity checks and transactional publication remain in force.
+- `gc/native.goose`: unchanged. Its separate `NG_TYPE_LIMIT` is 65,536 and is now the next managed-type limit.
+
+Reservation and failed group registration do not publish partial map entries or advance `type_count`; the existing rollback suite exercises repeated failed instantiations in one store. The existing linked-store roots suite exercises cross-module registration and use.
+
+## Gate results
+
+The build and focused gates used:
+
+```
+PATH=/data/workspace/tools:/data/workspace/tools/wabt-1.0.42/bin:$PATH
+GOOSE_HOME=/tmp/r8-fix/goose
+GOOSE_STDLIB=/data/workspace/tools/stdlib
+```
+
+- `make -j4`: PASS, 1 build / 0 failures.
+- `make gc-type-capacity-test`: PASS, 18 cases / 0 failures. Per release, debug, and three-byte build: early-managed 4,097 and 20,000; C1 IDs 4,095 and 4,096; C2 layout counts 4,095 and 4,096.
+- `build/goosegc-test`: PASS, 32 cases and 1,064,061 assertions / 0 failures.
+- `tests/test_wasm3_gc_runtime.py` with release and tiny validators/runners: PASS. Validation: 17 assertions per validator (6 accepts, 11 rejects), 0 failures; both execution runners passed the runtime matrix, 0 failures.
+- `tests/test_gc_abi2_graph.py build/starshine`: PASS, 4 worker configurations (1/2/4/8), each with a 100,001-node cycle / 0 failures.
+- `tests/test_gc_native.py build/gc-abi2-stress`: PASS, 28 checks / 0 failures.
+- `tests/test_wasm3_gc_rollback.py` with release/debug/tiny spec runners: PASS, 3 runners / 0 failures.
+- `tests/test_wasm3_gc_roots.py` with release/tiny runners: PASS, 2 runners / 0 failures, including linked-store coverage.
+- `make conformance`: PASS in release single-worker, release 8-worker, and three-byte 8-worker modes. Each mode checked 147 files, 1,717 acceptances, and 2,880 rejections; 0 failures. The corpus was cached/available, so the anticipated GitHub-DNS block did not apply.
+
+`make -k test` was also sampled but not used as a clean gate: it was stopped during the very long re-entry stress run. Before interruption it reproduced the known parallel-JIT helper-count failure and the two known Wago corpus failures. The pinned Wago coverage checkout was unavailable. It also observed a three-byte failed-instantiation-cleanup VmSize tolerance miss; focused rollback and roots suites passed. The instantiation-descriptor harness was not blocked on this run and passed in release, debug, and three-byte modes. Standing laptop known-reds (cached-body fixture, 15 Wasm 2 execution failures, compiler success-message assertion, and Redline oracle pin mismatch) were not chased.
+
+## Performance discipline
+
+This is the cheapest correct version: growth and its zero initialization happen only at type registration. No allocations, copies, hashing, scans, or recomputation were added to execution lookup paths. `wasm_gc_type` remains a bounds check followed by a direct indexed map read, and the collector type lookup remains directly indexed.
+
+## READY TO MEASURE
+
+Status: READY TO MEASURE
+
+Branch: `fix/typecap-c1c2`
+
+Head: the report-carrying branch head; implementation is commit `059d10f`.
+
+Perf-sensitive paths: registration-time type/map growth and execution-time direct type lookup.
+
+Proposed workloads: module load with 4,096-plus types (including the 20,000-type case), the GC real-program workloads, and the collector stress set.
